# BBQ Tofu Bowls

Based on [School Night Vegan - Easy Tofu Marinades](https://schoolnightvegan.com/home/easy-tofu-marinades) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260112215657/https://schoolnightvegan.com/home/easy-tofu-marinades/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Sticky BBQ Tofu

- [ ] 2 (14-ounce) blocks [extra-firm tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, pressed and cut into 1-inch cubes
- [ ] 3 tablespoons [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" }
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [vegan Worcestershire sauce]{ ing="vegan-worcestershire-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 tablespoon [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 3 tablespoons [light brown sugar]{ ing="light-brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [tomato puree]{ ing="tomato-puree" }
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [dark soy sauce]{ ing="dark-soy-sauce" } (or regular soy sauce)
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [water]{ ing="water" }

### Bowl Components

- [ ] 2 cups [long-grain rice]{ ing="long-grain-rice" } (white or brown)
- [ ] 3 cups [water]{ ing="water" } (4.5 cups for brown rice)
- [ ] 1 pound [broccoli florets]{ ing="broccoli-florets" } (or Brussels sprouts, halved)
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] [Salt and black pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" }
- [ ] 2 cups [corn kernels]{ ing="corn-kernels" } (fresh or frozen)
- [ ] 4 [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [toasted sesame seeds]{ ing="toasted-sesame-seeds" } (optional)

## Recipe

### Marinate the Tofu

1. Press [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } for at least 30 minutes to remove excess moisture, then cut into 1-inch cubes
1. In a bowl or ziplock bag, whisk together [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [Worcestershire sauce]{ ing="vegan-worcestershire-sauce" }, [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }, [brown sugar]{ ing="light-brown-sugar" }, [tomato puree]{ ing="tomato-puree" }, [dark soy sauce]{ ing="dark-soy-sauce" }, and [water]{ ing="water" }
1. Add [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } cubes and toss to coat. Refrigerate for minimum 30 minutes or up to overnight

### Cook the Rice

1. Rinse [rice]{ ing="long-grain-rice" } under cold [water]{ ing="water" } until water runs clear
1. Combine [rice]{ ing="long-grain-rice" } and [water]{ ing="water" } in a pot. Bring to a boil, reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer 15 minutes for white rice or 40-45 minutes for brown rice
1. Remove from heat and let sit covered for 10 minutes, then fluff with a fork

### Roast the Tofu and Vegetables

1. Heat oven to 425°F and line two baking sheets with parchment paper
1. Toss [broccoli florets]{ ing="broccoli-florets" } with [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }, salt, and [pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" } on one baking sheet
1. Remove [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } from marinade (reserve marinade) and spread on second baking sheet in a single layer
1. Roast both sheets for 15 minutes
1. Flip [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } pieces, toss broccoli, and roast another 10-15 minutes until tofu is caramelized and broccoli is crispy at edges
1. While [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } finishes roasting, heat reserved marinade in a small saucepan over medium heat until thickened, about 3-5 minutes. Toss tofu with thickened [sauce]{ ing="dark-soy-sauce" }

### Prepare Corn (Optional)

1. If using fresh corn, char in a dry skillet over high heat for 3-4 minutes until slightly blackened
1. If using frozen corn, thaw and pat dry, then char in skillet

### Assemble Bowls

1. Divide [rice]{ ing="long-grain-rice" } among bowls
1. Top with BBQ [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, roasted broccoli, and corn
1. Garnish with sliced [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" } and [sesame seeds]{ ing="toasted-sesame-seeds" }

## Notes

- **Meal prep advantage**: All components can be prepared in advance and stored separately for 4-5 days. Reheat tofu in oven at 375°F for 5-7 minutes to restore crispiness, or enjoy cold
- **Vegan Worcestershire substitute**: 2 Tbsp soy sauce + 1 Tbsp balsamic vinegar per 2 Tbsp Worcestershire
- **Dark soy sauce substitute**: Regular soy sauce + 1/4 tsp molasses or brown sugar per 1 Tbsp dark soy
- **Alternative vegetables**: Sweet potato cubes, cauliflower, or bell peppers work well with BBQ flavors
- **Sandwich option**: Use BBQ tofu in sandwiches with coleslaw and pickles on toasted buns
- **Air fryer method**: After marinating, air fry tofu at 400°F for 15-18 minutes, shaking basket halfway through. Toss with thickened marinade after cooking
- **For crispier tofu**: Toss marinated tofu with 1-2 tablespoons cornstarch before roasting
